  "tagline": "Oracle's long-running Java data grid, with a UPL-licensed Community Edition on GitHub.",
  "description": "Coherence is a partitioned, replicated in-memory data grid that Oracle acquired with Tangosol in 2007 and still ships with WebLogic. It provides distributed maps with queries, aggregations, entry processors, events and near caches, plus gRPC and REST access for non-Java clients. Since 2020 a Community Edition is developed in the open under the permissive UPL license, with calendar-versioned releases (26.07 in September 2026), while commercial Enterprise and Grid editions add features like federated caching. Recent releases add vector storage with HNSW indexes and Lucene-backed full-text search.",
